{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    res = []\n    while x > 0:\n        res.append(str(x % base))\n        x //= base\n    return ''.join(res[::-1])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the four preceding values needed for calculation: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    # These correspond to fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1) in the first iteration (i=4)\n    f_n_minus_4 = 0 # fib4(0)\n    f_n_minus_3 = 0 # fib4(1)\n    f_n_minus_2 = 2 # fib4(2)\n    f_n_minus_1 = 0 # fib4(3)\n\n    # Iteratively compute fib4(i) for i from 4 up to n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib4 = f_n_minus_1 + f_n_minus_2 + f_n_minus_3 + f_n_minus_4\n        # Shift the values for the next iteration\n        f_n_minus_4 = f_n_minus_3\n        f_n_minus_3 = f_n_minus_2\n        f_n_minus_2 = f_n_minus_1\n        f_n_minus_1 = current_fib4\n    \n    # After the loop, f_n_minus_1 holds the value of fib4(n)\n    return f_n_minus_1"}
